(this was extracted from [this post draft](/blog/mojo-memory-safety))


# Where this could go: Argument Paths

There are still problems to solve, of course.


We've enabled local mutable aliasing, and we have return ref origin paths to help us with local mutable aliasing, but there's a gap: we aren't able to extract out helper functions anymore.


For example, if we start with this:


<ignore>
```mojo
@fieldwise_init
struct Wing(Copyable, Movable):
    var span: Int

@fieldwise_init
struct Tail(Copyable, Movable):
    var length: Int

@fieldwise_init
struct Bird:
    var left: Wing
    var right: Wing
    var tail: Tail

    fn get_weight(self):
        return left.span + right.span + tail.length

fn main():
    var bird = Bird(Wing(10), Wing(20), Tail(15))
    ref tail_ref = bird.tail
    tail_ref.length += bird.get_weight()
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #c9d1d9">@</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">fieldwise&#95;init</span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">struct</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ffa657">Wing</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Copyable</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Movable</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">span</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Int</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">@</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">fieldwise&#95;init</span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">struct</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ffa657">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Copyable</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Movable</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">length</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Int</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">@</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">fieldwise&#95;init</span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">struct</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ffa657">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">left</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Wing</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">right</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Wing</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Tail</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">get&#95;weight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">self</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">return</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">left</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">span</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">+</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">right</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">span</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">+</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">length</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">main</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Wing</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">10</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Wing</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">20</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">15</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">length</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">+=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">get&#95;weight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span></code></pre>


...and we try to split the `main` into two functions:


<ignore>
```mojo
fn main():
    var bird = Bird(Wing(10), Wing(20), Tail(15))
    ref tail_ref = bird.tail
    evolve(bird, tail_ref)

fn evolve(bird: Bird, mut tail_ref: Tail):
    tail_ref.length += bird.get_weight()
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">main</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Wing</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">10</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Wing</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">20</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">15</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">evolve</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">evolve</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> mut </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">length</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">+=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">get&#95;weight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span></code></pre>


we unfortunately get this error:


<ignore>
```mojo
fn main():
    var bird = Bird(Wing(10), Wing(20), Tail(15))
    ref tail_ref = bird.tail

    # error: argument of 'evolve' call allows writing a memory location previously readable through another aliased argument
    evolve(bird, tail_ref)
    #     ^~~~~  ~~~~~~~~
    # note: 'bird.tail' value is passed through aliasing 'mut' argument

fn evolve(bird: Bird, mut tail_ref: Tail):
    tail_ref.length += bird.get_weight()
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">main</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Wing</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">10</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Wing</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">20</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">15</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> error: argument of &#039;evolve&#039; call allows writing a memory location previously readable through another aliased argument</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">evolve</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e">     ^~~~~  ~~~~~~~~</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> note: &#039;bird.tail&#039; value is passed through aliasing &#039;mut&#039; argument</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">evolve</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> mut </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">length</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">+=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">get&#95;weight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span></code></pre>


As far as I know, this is the only time we can't extract a local scope into a helper function.


In this way, Mojo _code_ can have mutable aliasing, but Mojo _programs_ do not. Mojo programs will largely be shaped like Rust programs, because this benefit is foiled at function call boundaries.


Luckily, there is a way we can express this to the compiler nicely.


"Aha! Is the answer that we make `evolve` take in a single argument `mut bird: Bird`?"

Good question! But no, that's not what I'm talking about. That does work in simple cases, but it doesn't scale well: when we try that workaround on anything larger than a simple function, we incur extra complexity, performance problems, and architectural risks.


Before I explain the real solution, I'll show you those scaling problems with a couple examples: one from a simple game, and one from Google Earth.


Buckle up, because this blog is about to live up to its name!


(Or you can [skip to the real solution](#argument-paths))


## Example: A Simple Game

Let's take this example.

In a little roguelike game, we might have a `plan` method that is purely for the `Entity` to re-orient themselves, and figure out what they want to do (but not actually do it yet).


Here's the `plan` method, plus the structs it interacts with.

There's a certain problem with it, which I'll explain below.


<ignore>
```mojo
struct PursueDirective:
    enemy_id: Int
    enemy_last_seen_loc: Location
    path: List[Location]

struct LoiterDirective: pass  # empty

alias Directive = Variant[LoiterDirective, PursueDirective]

struct Entity:
    loc: Location
    is_blinded: Bool
    directive: Directive

struct World:
    entities: List[Entity]
    tiles: List[List[Entity]]


# Entity looks around and thinks and decides their objective
fn plan(read world: World, mut entity: Entity):
    # If there's an existing directive, check it and see if it even makes sense anymore.
    # In which case, set to loiter.
    match entity.directive:
        case LoiterDirective as walk:
            pass
        case PursueDirective as pursue:
            enemy_loc = world.entities[enemy_id].loc

            if can_see_loc(world, entity, enemy_loc):
                pursue.enemy_last_seen_at = enemy_loc
                # Store the path to the enemy. Keep the path around so we
                # have something to follow if we lose sight of the enemy.
                pursue.path = find_path(entity.loc, enemy_loc)
                if len(pursue.path) == 0:
                    # We see them but can't get to them, abort.
                    entity.directive = LoiterDirective()
                if not world.tiles[pursue.path[0]].walkable:
                    # Next step is unwalkable for some reason, abort.
                    entity.directive = LoiterDirective()
                else: # There's a path to the enemy!
                    pass # Keep pursuing!
            else: # Can't see the player.
                if entity.loc == pursue.enemy_last_seen_at:
                    # We reached where we last saw them. Give up.
                    entity.directive = LoiterDirective()
                else:
                    pass # Keep pursuing!
    ...

fn can_see_loc(world: World, entity: Entity, loc: Location) -> Bool:
    return (
        not is_blinded(entity) and
        has_line_of_sight(world, entity.loc, loc)
    )
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #ff7b72">struct</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ffa657">PursueDirective</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">enemy&#95;id</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Int</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">enemy&#95;last&#95;seen&#95;loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Location</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">path</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">List</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">&#91;</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Location</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">]</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">struct</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ffa657">LoiterDirective</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">pass</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">  </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> empty</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">alias</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Directive</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Variant</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">&#91;</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">LoiterDirective</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">PursueDirective</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">]</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">struct</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ffa657">Entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Location</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">is&#95;blinded</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Bool</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">directive</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Directive</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">struct</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ffa657">World</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">entities</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">List</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">&#91;</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">]</span>
