<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">return</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">not</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">is&#95;blinded</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">and</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">has&#95;line&#95;of&#95;sight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">world</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span></code></pre>


So let's see the problem. Look at the signature again:


<ignore>
```mojo
fn plan(read world: World, mut entity: Entity):
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">plan</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">read </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">world</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">World</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> mut </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span></code></pre>


That `entity` is _inside_ the `World`. So, Mojo rejects this:

(show error)


The classic Rust solution would be to refactor `plan` to give it *mutable access to the entire World* (`&mut World`) and a handle (`entity_id`) that we can use to find the `Entity` in the `World`.


```rs
// Entity looks around and thinks and decides their objective
fn plan(world: &mut World, entity_id: usize) {
    let entity_read = &world.entities[entity_id];

    // if there's an existing directive, check it and see if it even makes sense anymore.
    // In which case, set to loiter.
    // TODO: try to get rid of this clone. then we'll have a mut ref supposedly and we can overwrite it
    match entity_read.directive.clone() {
        LoiterDirective => {}
        PursueDirective(existing_pursue) => {
            let enemy_loc = world.entities[existing_pursue.enemy_id].loc.clone();

            if can_see_loc(&world, entity_read, &enemy_loc) {
                // we store path to the enemy. keep the path around so we
                // dont have to recalculate it every turn, just recalculate
                // if we run into something.
                let new_path = find_path(&world, &entity_read.loc, &enemy_loc);
                if new_path.steps.len() == 0 {
                    // we see them but can't get to them. loiter instead.
                    // need to re-fetch because we need to mutate.
                    // Mention: ironically, this is why vale did its gen ref thing.
                    let entity_mut = &mut world.entities[entity_id];
                    entity_mut.directive = LoiterDirective;
                } else if !world.tile_at(&new_path.steps[0]).walkable {
                    // next step is unwalkable for some reason, stop
                    // need to re-fetch because we need to mutate.
                    let entity_mut = &mut world.entities[entity_id];
                    entity_mut.directive = LoiterDirective;
                } else { // there's a path to the enemy
                    // keep pursuing
                    let entity_mut = &mut world.entities[entity_id];
                    entity_mut.directive = PursueDirective(Pursue {
                        enemy_id: existing_pursue.enemy_id,
                        enemy_last_seen_loc: enemy_loc,
                        path: new_path
                    });
                }
            } else { // can't see the player
                if entity_read.loc == existing_pursue.enemy_last_seen_loc {
                    // we're where we last saw them. give up.
                    // need to re-fetch because we need to mutate.
                    let entity_mut = &mut world.entities[entity_id];
                    entity_mut.directive = LoiterDirective;
                } else {
                    // keep pursuing
                    let entity_mut = &mut world.entities[entity_id];
                    entity_mut.directive = PursueDirective(Pursue {
                        enemy_id: existing_pursue.enemy_id,
                        enemy_last_seen_loc: enemy_loc,
                        path: existing_pursue.path
                    });
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

fn can_see_loc(world: &World, entity: &Entity, loc: &Location) -> bool {
    return !entity.is_blinded &&
        world.has_line_of_sight(&entity.loc, loc);
}

// TODO: change from usize to generational_index
```


We needed to hand in a `&mut World` because:

 * We need mutable access to something inside it.
 * We need access to `World` for various functions (`can_see_loc`, etc.).


However, we just introduced two problems:

 1. We just made it slower: the borrow checker forced us to do `let entity_read = &world.entities[entity_id];` to look up the entity. Unfortunate, because the caller likely already had a reference handy.
 2. We made it slower again: the borrow checker forced us to add an extra `let entity_mut = &mut world.entities[entity_id];` lookup on each path because we couldn't use our `entity_read` to mutate.
 3. `plan` now has mutable access to the entire World.


Let's talk about that last one. This is problematic for two reasons:

 * We risk architectural violations: we now risk someone modifying something outside of this entity, if they didn't understand that `plan` is only supposed to modify this single unit's intentions, it's not supposed to modify anything else in the World.
 * It's viral: it forces all of `plan`'s callers to receive a `&mut World`, so they can give it to `plan`.


In other words, it's a viral architectural risk.


Don't get me wrong, the borrow checker is great and a net positive. But this is a very strong drawback.


And unfortunately, Mojo is in the same situation.


...or is it?


Perhaps not!


There's nothing inherently unsafe with the original code. This is one of those cases where the borrow checker just doesn't have the right information, and therefore has to conservatively reject a valid program.


So what is the right information?


It's one simple addition, to tell the compiler what makes it safe: an *argument origin path.*


We'd simply add `[world.entities]` to the `entity` argument:


<ignore>
```mojo
fn plan(read world: World, mut [world.entities] entity: Entity):
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">plan</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">read </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">world</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">World</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> mut &#91;world.entities] </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span></code></pre>


That's it.


The rest of the function doesn't need to change. I'll show the full function anyway for reference, and then I'll explain how it works below.


<ignore>
```mojo
# Entity looks around and thinks and decides their objective
fn plan(read world: World, mut [world.entities] entity: Entity):
    # if there's an existing directive, check it and see if it even makes sense anymore.
    # In which case, set to loiter.
    match entity.directive:
        case LoiterDirective as walk:
            pass
        case PursueDirective as pursue:
            # convenient: we're not holding an enemy_ref. but if we were,
            # it might be fine because of origin path tracking.
            enemy_loc = world.entities[enemy_id].loc

            if can_see_loc(world, entity, enemy_loc):
                pursue.enemy_last_seen_at = enemy_loc
                # we store path to the enemy. keep the path around so we
                # dont have to recalculate it every turn, just recalculate
                # if we run into something.
                pursue.path = find_path(entity.loc, enemy_loc)
                if len(pursue.path) == 0:
                    # we see them but can't get to them. loiter instead.
                    entity.directive = LoiterDirective()
                if not world.tiles[pursue.path[0]].walkable:
                    # next step is unwalkable for some reason, stop
                    entity.directive = LoiterDirective()
                else: # there's a path to the enemy
                    pass # keep pursuing
            else: # can't see the player
                if entity.loc == pursue.enemy_last_seen_at:
                    # we're where we last saw them. give up.
                    entity.directive = LoiterDirective()
                else:
                    # keep pursuing
                    pass

fn can_see_loc(world: World, entity: Entity, loc: Location) -> Bool:
    return (
        not is_blinded(entity) and
        has_line_of_sight(world, entity.loc, loc)
    )

```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> Entity looks around and thinks and decides their objective</span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">plan</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">read </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">world</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">World</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> mut &#91;world.entities] </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> if there&#039;s an existing directive, check it and see if it even makes sense anymore.</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> In which case, set to loiter.</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">match</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">directive</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">case</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">LoiterDirective</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">as</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">walk</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">pass</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">case</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">PursueDirective</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">as</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">pursue</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> convenient: we&#039;re not holding an enemy&#95;ref. but if we were,</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> it might be fine because of origin path tracking.</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">enemy&#95;loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">world</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">entities</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">&#91;</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">enemy&#95;id</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">]</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">loc</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">if</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">can&#95;see&#95;loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">world</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">enemy&#95;loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">pursue</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">enemy&#95;last&#95;seen&#95;at</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">enemy&#95;loc</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> we store path to the enemy. keep the path around so we</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> dont have to recalculate it every turn, just recalculate</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> if we run into something.</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">pursue</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">path</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">find&#95;path</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">enemy&#95;loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">if</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">len</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">pursue</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">path</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">==</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">0</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                    </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> we see them but can&#039;t get to them. loiter instead.</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">directive</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">LoiterDirective</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">if</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">not</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">world</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tiles</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">&#91;</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">pursue</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">path</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">&#91;</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">0</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">]</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">]</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">walkable</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                    </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> next step is unwalkable for some reason, stop</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">directive</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">LoiterDirective</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">else</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> there&#039;s a path to the enemy</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">pass</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> keep pursuing</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">else</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> can&#039;t see the player</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">if</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">==</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">pursue</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">enemy&#95;last&#95;seen&#95;at</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                    </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> we&#039;re where we last saw them. give up.</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">directive</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">LoiterDirective</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">else</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                    </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> keep pursuing</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">                    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">pass</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">can&#95;see&#95;loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">world</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">World</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Location</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">-&gt;</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Bool</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">return</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">not</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">is&#95;blinded</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">and</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">has&#95;line&#95;of&#95;sight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">world</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">loc</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span></span></code></pre>


So how does this work? All we did was change the signature:


<ignore>
```mojo
fn plan(read world: World, mut [world.entities] entity: Entity):
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">plan</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">read </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">world</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">World</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> mut &#91;world.entities] </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Entity</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span></code></pre>


How did that one addition of `[world.entities]` make this entire thing memory safe?


It's because the compiler now knows two things:

 * The `entity` reference is pointing at one of the entities in `world.entities`. And therefore...
 * If we ever temporarily turn the `entity` reference immutable (easy), then the entire `world` is temporarily immutable.


And suddenly, with that last item there, we've solved the problems that led to the harmful `&mut World` workaround:

 * We have mutable access to the `Entity`. No need for `&mut World`!
 * We have immutable access to `World` for various functions (`can_see_loc`, etc.). No need for `&mut World`!


This is much better, because now our type system is helping us maintain our architecture, instead of working against us.


Okay, but this is just a toy example, let's hear about a real use case!


(TODO: doesn't this also enable better error messages?)
(TODO: reference Niko's View Types post wherever possible)


## Example: Google Earth

Long ago, in the earlier days of [Google Earth](https://earth.google.com/web/), we were constantly facing state management challenges, because Earth was such a large app with such complex requirements, and we weren't that principled about it.


(And yes, before you ask, we couldn't eliminate this state. This was _inherent_ state. Client-side apps can't avoid inherent state, you just have to be disciplined about how you handle it.)


Some of these problems got so complicated and spaghetti-ish that there were some bugs that took _weeks_ to fix.

These problems seemed to rhyme, and my spidey sense was tingling. I eventually found the common pattern in all of these problems:

 * Presenter A modifies the AppState.
    * Presenter B observes this, and modifies the AppState in response.
 * Presenter A reads the AppState, found it in a completely unexpected state, and crashed.


We then put some constraints on our system [#statemanager] which completely eliminated this entire class of bugs. One of them was this:

> AppState methods could read and mutate the AppState, but could only _read_ the surrounding world.


This was in C++, so we simply gave AppState some const references to the other subsystems.

In Rust, we might have needed the same workaround:

 * Take a &mut App and suddenly have mutable access to *everything*
 * Take a &mut self, and & refs to everything else (very verbose, there are a lot, cant call other methods)

(Or we could take in 20 subsystems in as arguments)


And Mojo would have the same problems.


But with argument paths, we could make a function like this:


<ignore>
```mojo
struct App:
    var document_manager: DocumentManager
    var app_state: AppState
    var network_requester: NetworkRequester
    var lfs: LocalFileSystem
    ... # About 15 more

    fn can_show_document(self, document_id: Int) -> bool:
        return (
            self.network_requester.ready() and
            self.document_manager.ready() and
            self.document_manager.document_loaded(document_id)
        )

fn open_document_view(
    read app: App,
    mut [app.state] app_state: AppState,
    document_id: Int  # TODO: I think this could even be a ref now?
) -> Bool:
    app_state.currently_open_card_id = None
    app_state.legend_is_open = False
    app_state.currently_open_document_id = document_id
    if app.can_show_document(document_id):
        app_state.current_view = CurrentView::Document
        return True
    else:
        return False
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #ff7b72">struct</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ffa657">App</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">document&#95;manager</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">DocumentManager</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">app&#95;state</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">AppState</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">network&#95;requester</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">NetworkRequester</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">lfs</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">LocalFileSystem</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">...</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> About 15 more</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">can&#95;show&#95;document</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">self</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">document&#95;id</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Int</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">-&gt;</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ffa657">bool</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">return</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">self</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">network&#95;requester</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">ready</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">and</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">self</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">document&#95;manager</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">ready</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">and</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">self</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">document&#95;manager</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">document&#95;loaded</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">document&#95;id</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">open&#95;document&#95;view</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    read </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">app</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">App</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    mut &#91;app.state] </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">app&#95;state</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">AppState</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">document&#95;id</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Int</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">  </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">TODO</span><span style="color: #8b949e">: I think this could even be a ref now?</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">-&gt;</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Bool</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">app&#95;state</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">currently&#95;open&#95;card&#95;id</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">None</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">app&#95;state</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">legend&#95;is&#95;open</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">False</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">app&#95;state</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">currently&#95;open&#95;document&#95;id</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">document&#95;id</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">if</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">app</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">can&#95;show&#95;document</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">document&#95;id</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">app&#95;state</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">current&#95;view</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">CurrentView</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Document</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">return</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">True</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">else</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">return</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">False</span></code></pre>


(This is of course a simplified version of the actual Google Earth logic, [# For example, there were a few more AppState methods that would be called when the `network_requester` and `document_manager` were all ready.] but you get the idea.)


Note how `open_document_view` is reading the `app` with `app.can_show_document(document_id)`, yet it also has a `mut app_state`. This is possible because of the `app` argument's `[app.state]` origin path.


This is much better, because now our type system is helping us maintain our architecture, instead of working against us.


(TODO: doesn't this also enable better error messages?)
(TODO: reference Niko's View Types post wherever possible)


<slice>
#statemanager: The complete list of constraints:

 * If Presenter A needs to modify Presenter B's state ("cross-cutting mutation"), move that state into the central AppState class.
 * All cross-cutting mutation logic (`OpenDocumentView` which closes CardView, `SetShownCard` which hides the LegendView, etc.) should be in an AppState method.
 * When a presenter observes a change, it cannot ask AppState to mutate anything in response.
 * AppState methods could only mutate AppState, but could also _read_ the surrounding world.
</slice>


## Argument Paths

In all three of those examples, we added *argument origin paths* to let us access a mutable part of an otherwise-immutable whole.


We helped the compiler understand that `evolve` was memory-safe by specifying `tail_ref`'s origin path was `[bird.tail]`:


<ignore>
```mojo
fn main():
    var bird = Bird(Wing(10), Wing(20), Tail(15))
    ref tail_ref = bird.tail
    evolve(bird, tail_ref)

fn evolve(bird: Bird, mut [bird.tail] tail_ref: Tail):
    tail_ref.length += bird.get_weight()
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">main</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Wing</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">10</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Wing</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">20</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">15</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">evolve</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">evolve</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> mut &#91;bird.tail] </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">length</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">+=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">get&#95;weight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span></code></pre>


