So how does this actually work under the hood?


Let's look at the first example:


<ignore>
```mojo
fn main():
    var bird = Bird(Wing(10), Wing(20), Tail(15))
    ref tail_ref = bird.tail
    evolve(bird, tail_ref)

fn evolve(bird: Bird, mut [bird.tail] tail_ref: Tail):
    tail_ref.length += bird.get_weight()
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">main</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Wing</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">10</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Wing</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">20</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">15</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">evolve</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span></span>
<span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">evolve</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> mut &#91;bird.tail] </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">length</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">+=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">get&#95;weight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span></code></pre>


That `evolve` is equivalent to this, which uses a temporary variable:


<ignore>
```mojo
fn evolve(bird: Bird, mut [bird.tail] tail_ref: Tail):
    var weight = bird.get_weight()
    tail_ref.length += weight
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">evolve</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> mut &#91;bird.tail] </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">weight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">get&#95;weight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">length</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">+=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">weight</span></code></pre>


Now I'll add a few comments that explain the compiler's thinking:


<ignore>
```mojo
fn evolve(bird: Bird, mut [bird.tail] tail_ref: Tail):
    var weight =
        borrow_imm tail_ref {
            # Begin temporary scope, in which `tail_ref` is an immutable borrow.
            # Now, `bird` *and* everything inside it (`tail_ref`) is immutable.
            # We can now pass an immutable `bird` to `get_weight`.
            bird.get_weight()
            # End temporary scope, `tail_ref` becomes mutable again.
        }
    # `tail_ref` is mutable here, so add to its `length`.
    tail_ref.length += weight
```
</ignore>


<pre style="background-color: black; padding: 16px; font-size: 80%; overflow-x: auto;"><code class="nohighlight"><span style="color: #ff7b72">fn</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">evolve</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #79c0ff">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">,</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> mut &#91;bird.tail] </span><span style="color: #79c0ff">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">Tail</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">:</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">var</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">weight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">=</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">borrow&#95;imm</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">{</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> Begin temporary scope, in which `tail&#95;ref` is an immutable borrow.</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> Now, `bird` *and* everything inside it (`tail&#95;ref`) is immutable.</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> We can now pass an immutable `bird` to `get&#95;weight`.</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">bird</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #d2a8ff">get&#95;weight</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">(</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">)</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">            </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> End temporary scope, `tail&#95;ref` becomes mutable again.</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">        </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">}</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #8b949e">#</span><span style="color: #8b949e"> `tail&#95;ref` is mutable here, so add to its `length`.</span>
<span style="color: #c9d1d9">    </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">tail&#95;ref</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">.</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">length</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #ff7b72">+=</span><span style="color: #c9d1d9"> </span><span style="color: #c9d1d9">weight</span></code></pre>


In other words, when we try to pass something (`bird`) to a function (`get_weight`) that wants to receive it immutably (the `read` in `fn get_weight(read self)`), we temporarily turn all of its "contained references" (`tail_ref`) immutable, so the entire thing (`bird`) is immutable.


### Limitations

There are some limitations to this mechanism, of course:

 * We can't pass an object as both `read` and `mut` (though we can pass it as `mut` and `mut`).
 * (any other limitations?)


First, we can't pass the same object as both `read` and `mut`. We can't do this:


<ignore>
```mojo
fn main():
    var bird = Bird(Wing(10), Wing(20), Tail(15))
    ref tail_ref = bird.tail
    evolve(bird, tail_ref, tail_ref)

fn evolve(
    bird: Bird,
    read [bird.tail] tail_a: Tail,
    mut [bird.tail] tail_b: Tail
):
    tail_b.length += bird.get_weight() + tail_a.length
```
</ignore>


