And it should compose well with the existing origin checking machinery.


And if we want to, we can pass them both as `read` (this works today):


<ignore>
```mojo
fn main():
    var bird = Bird(Wing(10), Wing(20), Tail(15))
    ref tail_ref = bird.tail
    evolve(bird, tail_ref, tail_ref)

fn evolve(
    bird: Bird,
    read tail_a: Tail,
    read tail_b: Tail
):
    print(tail_b.length + bird.get_weight() + tail_a.length)
```
</ignore>


